# 94. The Most Important Three Backward Equations

If you forget everything else, remember these three structural rules.

### Rule 1: Product

If

$$
y=uv,
$$

then:

$$
\bar u=\bar yv
$$

and

$$
\bar v=\bar yu.
$$

The LSTM cell update is just repeated application of this rule.

---

### Rule 2: Activation

If

$$
y=\sigma(x),
$$

then:

$$
\bar x=\bar y\,y(1-y).
$$

If

$$
y=\tanh(x),
$$

then:

$$
\bar x=\bar y(1-y^2).
$$

---

### Rule 3: Affine transformation

If:

$$
y=Wx+b,
$$

then:

$$
\boxed{
\bar W=\bar yx^T
}
$$

$$
\boxed{
\bar b=\bar y
}
$$

$$
\boxed{
\bar x=W^T\bar y
}
$$

The entire LSTM backward pass is essentially these three rules applied to the computational graph.

