# 96. Suggested C Structure

A conceptual structure could be:

```c
typedef struct {
    int input_size;
    int hidden_size;

    double *W;
    double *b;

    double *dW;
    double *db;

    double *h;
    double *c;
} LSTM;
```

For BPTT, the cache would normally be an array indexed by time:

```c
typedef struct {
    double *x;
    double *z;

    double *f;
    double *i;
    double *g;
    double *o;

    double *c;
    double *h;
} LSTMCache;
```

The exact memory layout is an implementation decision.

---

# 97. Row-Major Flattening

C does not natively provide multidimensional mathematical matrices in the way a numerical library does.

You can flatten:

$$
W_{ij}
$$

into:

```text
W[i * cols + j]
```

where:

```text
cols = H + D
```

Therefore:

```c
W[i * cols + j]
```

represents:

$$
W_{ij}.
$$

---

# 98. Matrix-Vector Multiplication

For:

$$
a=Wz+b
$$

the C equivalent is conceptually:

```c
for (int i = 0; i < 4 * H; i++) {
    a[i] = b[i];

    for (int j = 0; j < H + D; j++) {
        a[i] += W[i * (H + D) + j] * z[j];
    }
}
```

This is exactly:

$$
a_i
=
b_i+
\sum_jW_{ij}z_j.
$$

---

# 99. Outer Product for the Weight Gradient

We derived:

$$
\bar W=\bar az^T.
$$

Therefore:

```c
for (int i = 0; i < 4 * H; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < H + D; j++) {
        dW[i * (H + D) + j]
            += da[i] * z[j];
    }
}
```

This is the direct implementation of:

$$
\frac{\partial L}{\partial W_{ij}}
=
\bar a_i z_j.
$$

---

# 100. Transposed Matrix Multiplication

For:

$$
\bar z=W^T\bar a,
$$

we have:

$$
\bar z_j
=
\sum_iW_{ij}\bar a_i.
$$

In C:

```c
for (int j = 0; j < H + D; j++) {
    dz[j] = 0.0;

    for (int i = 0; i < 4 * H; i++) {
        dz[j] += W[i * (H + D) + j] * da[i];
    }
}
```

Then:

```text
dz[0 ... H-1]
```

is the gradient for the previous hidden state.

And:

```text
dz[H ... H+D-1]
```

is the gradient for the current input.

---

# 101. The Implementation Order I Recommend

Do not immediately implement full BPTT.

Build it in stages.

## Stage 1

Implement:

```text
sigmoid
tanh
```

and test them.

---

## Stage 2

Implement:

```text
matrix_vector_multiply
```

and test it independently.

---

## Stage 3

Implement one LSTM forward step.

Verify every intermediate value.

---

## Stage 4

Implement one LSTM backward step.

Use finite differences to verify:

$$
dW
$$

and:

$$
db.
$$

---

## Stage 5

Add a sequence of two time steps.

Verify:

$$
dh_{t-1}
$$

and:

$$
dc_{t-1}.
