# 102. Final Mental Model

An LSTM is not fundamentally a mysterious new type of mathematics.

It is a computational graph built from:

* addition,
* multiplication,
* sigmoid,
* tanh,
* matrix multiplication,
* parameter sharing through time.

Its forward equations are:

$$
z=[h_{\text{prev}},x]
$$

$$
a=Wz+b
$$

$$
f=\sigma(a_f)
$$

$$
i=\sigma(a_i)
$$

$$
g=\tanh(a_g)
$$

$$
o=\sigma(a_o)
$$

$$
c=fc_{\text{prev}}+ig
$$

$$
h=o\tanh(c).
$$

Its backward equations are simply the chain rule applied backward:

$$
\bar h
\rightarrow
(\bar o,\bar c)
$$

$$
\bar c
\rightarrow
(\bar f,\bar i,\bar g,\bar c_{\text{prev}})
$$

$$
(\bar f,\bar i,\bar g,\bar o)
\rightarrow
(\bar a_f,\bar a_i,\bar a_g,\bar a_o)
$$

$$
\bar a
\rightarrow
(\bar W,\bar b,\bar z)
$$

$$
\bar z
\rightarrow
(\bar h_{\text{prev}},\bar x).
$$

Across time, the same parameters are reused, so:

$$
\boxed{
dW=\sum_t dW_t
}
$$

and:

$$
\boxed{
db=\sum_t db_t.
}
$$

The cell state carries a direct temporal pathway:

$$
c_{t-1}
\rightarrow
c_t
\rightarrow
c_{t+1}
\rightarrow\cdots
$$

whose local backward derivative is:

$$
\boxed{
\frac{\partial c_t}{\partial c_{t-1}}
=
f_t.
}
$$

That single equation explains much of the mathematical motivation behind the LSTM.

